[110.789209, "o", "Path(OUT/'report.md').write_text('''# Top-associated diphoton BDT categorization\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.789238, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.7893, "o", "## Introduction\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.789329, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.789601, "o", "Hadronic-only H→γγ top-associated categorization using ATLAS open data.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.789628, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.789749, "o", "## Data and Monte Carlo Samples\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.789777, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.7902, "o", "Only nominal ggH, VBF, WH, ZH, ggZH, ttH and tH MC and GamGam data were read; Sherpa/prompt continuum MC were excluded.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.790229, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.790375, "o", "## Object Definition and Event Selection\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.790404, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.791161, "o", "Two kinematic photons (pT>25 GeV, |η|<2.37) are required without photon tight-ID or isolation. Electrons/muons have pT>10 GeV; jets pT>25 GeV; b tags use quantile≥4. Hadronic is 0 leptons, ≥3 jets and ≥1 b tag.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.79119, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.79133, "o", "## Overview of the Analysis Strategy\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.79136, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.791716, "o", "A deterministic five-variable BDT uses ttH+tH as signal and ggH plus NTI sideband data as background.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.791765, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.791857, "o", "## Signal and Control Regions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.791886, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.792306, "o", "TI means both photons tight-ID and tight-isolation; NTI is its complement. TI signal-window observed data are blinded.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.792335, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.792392, "o", "## Cut Flow\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.79242, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.792639, "o", "See `cutflow.json` and ![](plots/preselection_channels.png).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.792667, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.792868, "o", "## Distributions in Signal and Control Regions\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.792896, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.793182, "o", "![](plots/preselection_mass.png) ![](plots/score_by_component_shape_bdt_v1.png)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.79321, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.793277, "o", "## Categorization\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.793304, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.793769, "o", "![](categorization/plots/category_expected_yields_36fb_v1.png) ![](categorization/plots/category_mgg_control_shapes_36fb_v1.png)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[110.793796, "o", "> "]
[110.793894, "o", "## Systematic Uncertainties\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.793922, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.794287, "o", "This starting point retains signed MC-weight bookkeeping; no nuisance systematic variations are fitted.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.794316, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.794428, "o", "## Statistical Interpretation\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.794457, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.794887, "o", "ROOT/PyROOT/RooFit workspace artifacts use the sideband-only, blinded Asimov strategy. Observed significance is blocked.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.794916, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.795222, "o", "![](fit/FIT1/plots/sidebands_background_fit.png) ![](fit/FIT1/plots/asimov_sb_fit.png)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.795252, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.795332, "o", "## Artifact Checklist\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.79536, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.795758, "o", "Machine-readable selection, training, inference, categorization, histograms and workspace manifests are present.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.795786, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.795843, "o", "## Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[110.795871, "o", "> "]
[110.796302, "o", "Expected 36 fb⁻¹ category yields use physical MC normalization and scaled NTI proxy, never class-balanced BDT weights.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[110.79633, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[110.796386, "o", "''')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
